                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "32f32c9d-f897-4453-a5e5-2526e29173ab",
                        "source_entry_id": "1645301d-8083-33ca-bcf2-cb487c85dd0a",
                        "source_sense_id": "234d09a3-cef8-38c1-8a62-9a00813c87eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "fatphobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fatphobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                        "entry_id": "d11c178a-f6ff-377d-8efc-b0f3713063b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fear and/or dislike of obese people and/or obesity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "954e73bd-e203-4c46-b6a7-cf4562094813",
                                                "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: sizeism, weightism"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8d7aa96-5414-4692-847f-61b22b0abb63",
                                                "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                                "text": "This is because medical authorities and proponents of public health are drawing from and amplifying the Western cultural fear and loathing of fatness, or fatphobia, with claims about a global 'obesity epidemic' (WHO 1998)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "360728db-5692-4832-97e9-924d59d0d666",
                                                "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                                "text": "Celebrity culture is intricately tied to fatphobia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a6e8cde-0153-4cca-96b4-d5f5493cf4cd",
                                                "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                                "text": "From long-lost high school friends found on Facebook to total strangers whom I'll probably never meet in person, I get asked questions from where to buy a good bra (my minimizer days are dead and buried) to how to deal with a spouse's fatphobia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7261bc04-54ae-4766-8892-8fcb914d3e74",
                                                "sense_id": "a036498d-110d-3554-ab6e-b139fc6cf53b",
                                                "text": "There are a lot of ways for people in the obese/eligible category to feel about it: […] Ambivalent about fatphobia in medicine working in their favor, for once."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6411228-b712-3f35-a82d-816034d69d83",
                                        "entry_id": "d11c178a-f6ff-377d-8efc-b0f3713063b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fear or obsessive avoidance of consuming fat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1abfc42a-0773-4fde-9b70-62385be14d5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "1645301d-8083-33ca-bcf2-cb487c85dd0a",
                        "source_sense_id": "234d09a3-cef8-38c1-8a62-9a00813c87eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "grossophobie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grossophobie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7d33df7-9a5e-3990-83b5-b12f010580dd",
                                        "entry_id": "a6f6bd8b-98eb-3f8a-8398-b0ef22991502",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Aversion ou attitude hostile envers les personnes en surpoids, grosses ou obèses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "970d58e1-61ee-4ee1-a5df-3ef3ca6d7730",
                                                "sense_id": "e7d33df7-9a5e-3990-83b5-b12f010580dd",
                                                "text": "Coup de gueule contre la grossophobie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4dacc1e2-cc2d-49d8-b948-b1133d552bca",
                                                "sense_id": "e7d33df7-9a5e-3990-83b5-b12f010580dd",
                                                "text": "La grossophobie ne se manifeste pas uniquement par des insultes ou des injonctions directes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad76d6c1-1b1e-4d93-ad41-4fd9ca93b103",
                                                "sense_id": "e7d33df7-9a5e-3990-83b5-b12f010580dd",
                                                "text": "Ce vendredi 15 décembre, sont organisés à Paris des événements pour lutter contre la grossophobie. Ce mot, vous l'avez peut-être déjà entendu car il est de plus en plus employé. Mais d'où vient-il et que signifie-t-il exactement? En français, il serait apparu pour la première fois en 1994 avec le livre d'Anne Zamberlan intitulé \"Coup de gueule contre la grossophobie\". Mais c'est bien plus récemment, avec l'ouvrage \"On ne naît pas grosse\" de Gabrielle Deydier, que le terme a été bien plus discuté en France."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d973a40-59d1-4f0f-bb4e-2389e2534b42",
                                                "sense_id": "e7d33df7-9a5e-3990-83b5-b12f010580dd",
                                                "text": "Et les thèmes comme la grossophobie, la xénophobie ou le harcèlement sont amenés sans que le roman perde de son humour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4511528-5c6e-4a2b-8a2c-971100c2af40",
                        "source_entry_id": "1645301d-8083-33ca-bcf2-cb487c85dd0a",
                        "source_sense_id": "234d09a3-cef8-38c1-8a62-9a00813c87eb",
                        "target_lang_word": "gordofobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gordofobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3f35593-bdb3-3874-86cb-c89d556406f7",
                                        "entry_id": "031254c6-9f72-34d8-b4b1-18b621c01ad1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rechazo y discriminación hacia personas con sobrepeso.^([cita requerida])"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90f86ddf-83ff-43cd-85a3-531385770e8f",
                                                "sense_id": "b3f35593-bdb3-3874-86cb-c89d556406f7",
                                                "text": "Si quieren un grado más de ridiculez, en términos de peso corporal, los flacos serían opresores de los gordos, y eso se llama gordofobia. Y esa categoría nuevamente no es un invento mío ni de un grupo más o menos radical. Es que ya hay universidades en Estados Unidos y de las más importantes que tienen por ejemplo departamentos de fat studies, o sea, estudios de la gordura. Y ya hay trabajos académicos de estudios de la gordura donde todo se basa en decir que hay un sistema de opresión de flacos contra gordos."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
